      "description": "Original MIT images, known transforms and projects by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors; no customer/third-party images. Three 192x128 captures occupy known x offsets 0/48/96 on a 288x128 canvas. Replay keeps each view independent with its original filename ticket, support and coordinate mapping. Intersection uses the exact common-valid support, including source-mask holes; Unbatch sends each image to an inspection. Native detail uses the factory and exact uint8 placement with masks enforced by the wrapper. Depth16 demonstrates preserved high-depth samples; native-depth and budget guards reject before warping. No-common is a deliberate failed replay using disjoint saved geometry (no physical timing/calibration claim). Source IDs/metadata assert identity, not synchronized exposures or physical camera correctness.",
